        "original_id": "c7b49354-3080-5ff5-8ba4-812f284167d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Damien Fahey, Craig Kilborn, Carson Daly, Julius Wu, Tom Snyder\n- Organizations: MTV, CBS, NBC, ESPN, Fox\n- Products: Total Request Live, The Late Late Show, The Daily Show, SportsCenter, Family Guy, Run, Chris, Run\n- Roles: writer, radio DJ, television host, MTV VJ, comedian, drummer, director\n\nFacts:\n- Craig Kilborn was born on August 24, 1962, and he is an American comedian, sports and political commentator, and television host.\n- Craig Kilborn was the original host of The Daily Show, a former anchor on ESPN's SportsCenter, and Tom Snyder's successor on CBS's The Late Late Show.\n- Damien Richard Fahey was born on June 1, 1980, and he is a writer for Family Guy, a radio DJ, a television host, a former MTV VJ, a comedian, and a drummer.\n- In 2002, Damien Fahey replaced Carson Daly as the host of MTV's Total Request Live after Carson Daly left the network to host his own late-night show on NBC.\n- In 2004, Damien Fahey was a guest host for CBS's The Late, Late Show after Craig Kilborn abruptly exited, and Damien Fahey was believed to be one of four finalists for the permanent role.\n- Run, Chris, Run aired on Fox in the United States on May 15, 2016, and the episode was written by Damien Fahey and directed by Julius Wu.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
